    {
      "id": "9acf55e1-2962-584d-a0f4-1b3d193f2b0b",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -620,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 500,
        "height": 860,
        "content": "## Respond instantly to real estate leads\n\nSpeed to lead wins listings and sales: this workflow answers every enquiry within seconds, 24/7, and tells you which ones to call first.\n\n### How it works\n1. Your website form, portal parser or Zapier-style hook posts the enquiry to the **webhook**.\n2. The lead is normalized (any field names), validated and **scored 0-100** \u2014 phone, timeline, budget, property reference and financing keywords raise the score.\n3. It is saved in Google Sheets; repeat enquiries update the same row (stable Lead ID).\n4. The lead gets a personalized email for buying, selling or renting, with your booking link.\n5. **Hot** leads trigger an instant alert to you. The form receives a JSON answer.\n\n### Setup\n- Connect **Gmail** and **Google Sheets** credentials.\n- Fill the **Config** node: Sheet ID, agency, name, email, phone, booking link, score thresholds.\n- Uses one Google Sheet with three tabs \u2014 **Leads**, **Listings**, **Viewings** \u2014 shared by the whole Real Estate Automation Kit (column list in the README).\n- Point your form to the production webhook URL.\n\n### Customization tips\n- Edit the email texts and scoring weights in **Normalize and score lead**.\n- Swap the agent alert for Slack, Telegram or Twilio SMS."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
